    {
      "invariant_id": "r_overflow_carry_repairs_leading_digit",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "include/fmt/format-inl.h",
      "function": "fmt::v7::detail::fallback_format",
      "line": 2594,
      "operands": [
        "buf[0]",
        "static_cast<int>('1')"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "buf[0]",
        "right": "static_cast<int>('1')"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_repair_leading_digit",
      "fine_trace_step": 8,
      "description": "Root cause. When rounding propagates a carry past the most significant generated digit, the fallback formatter increments the exponent but repairs the leading digit with `'0'` instead of `'1'`. For the staged `9.5f` / `\"{:.0e}\"` witness, that wrong `'0'` is later stripped away entirely, leaving a zero-digit buffer that the exponent-format writer cannot handle. The fix changes this exact assignment to `buf[0] = '1';`."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_copy_range_sink_receives_reversed_bounds",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "include/fmt/format.h",
      "function": "fmt::v7::detail::copy_str",
      "line": 574,
      "operands": [
        "digits_ + num_digits_",
        "digits_ + 1"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": "digits_ + num_digits_",
        "right": "digits_ + 1"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_copy_range_is_reversed",
      "fine_trace_step": 12,
      "description": "Closest project sink to the ASan crash. `copy_str()` consumes the invalid source range built by `float_writer::prettify()` when `num_digits_ == 0`, so `std::copy` reads sequential bytes from the stack `memory_buffer` until the iterator reaches the first byte past the object."
    },
